--- The math reductions, shapes, selection and element-wise functions are
--- rows of the builtin table (docs/bug-classes.md §4). A number and a
--- tensor share one rule: sign[0.0] was 1 compiled, from Rust's signum,
--- and 0 interpreted. An axis out of range, a reshape that does not fill,
--- and a transpose of a vector are the reason one function gives both
--- modes, where a kernel asserted.
use math
log[sign[0.0]]
log[sign[0 - 2.5]]
log[sign[[0.0, 3.0]]]
log[exp[0]]
log[ln[[1.0]]]
m = [[1.0, 2.0], [3.0, 4.0]]
log[sum[m]]
log[sum[m, 1]]
log[max[m, 0]]
log[argmax[[3.0, 9.0, 1.0]]]
log[topk[[3.0, 9.0, 1.0], 2]]
log[reshape[m, 4]]
log[transpose[m]]
log[clip[[0.5, 2.0], 0, 1]]
log[where[[1.0, 0.0], [5.0, 6.0], [7.0, 8.0]]]
log[transpose[[1.0, 2.0]]]
log['not reached']
